      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we first need to find the volume of each cube.\nThe volume of a cube is given by the formula V = s^3, where s is the length of one edge of the cube.\nFor the cube with edge length six inches, the volume is V = 6^3 = 216 cubic inches.\nTo convert this volume to cubic feet, we divide by 12^3 = 1728 cubic inches, so the volume is 216/1728 = 1/8 cubic feet.\nThe volume of a cube with edge length one foot is V = 1^3 = 1 cubic foot.\nTherefore, the ratio of the volume of the cube with edge length six inches to the volume of the cube with edge length one foot is 1/8:1 or \\boxed{1/8}.",
